course: dictionary
lesson: 14136
title: Amazing words: miraculous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Miraculous describes something so lucky and amazing that it seems almost impossible. Look at the words around it for clues. «The firefighter pulled the boy from the burning car, and he had only a scratch. It was miraculous.» A scratch after a crash like that is surprising, so miraculous must mean amazing and hard to explain.
explain: Use the swap check. Put «amazing» in place of miraculous: «It was amazing that he had only a scratch.» It still makes sense, so it is a good match. Miraculous is stronger, though. It suggests the good result happened against all the odds.
explain: Doctors and stories use the word too: «The patient made a miraculous recovery after weeks in hospital.» Recovery means getting better, so miraculous means she got better when nobody expected it. Useful phrases to remember are miraculous escape and miraculous recovery.
fact: Miraculous is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in a miraculous escape.
fact: «Miraculous» means like a miracle: amazing and hard to explain.
fact: «Miraculous» can also mean done through the power of God, a meaning found in religious writing.
fact: «Miraculous» can mean very good or surprising in its effect, as in «a miraculous cure».
fact: Words close in meaning include amazing and incredible, but miraculous suggests luck against the odds.
exercise: «The goalkeeper made a miraculous save in the last minute.» What does miraculous mean here? | Ordinary and easy | Loud and angry | *Amazing and hard to explain | Very slow
exercise: «Mum said it was miraculous that the cake did not burn.» What does miraculous suggest about the cake? | *It was lucky and surprising that it did not burn | It was too small | It was badly burnt | It was eaten quickly
exercise: Ella says miraculous means the same as boring. Is she right? | Yes, it means boring and slow | Yes, it means the same as tired | *No, miraculous means amazing and surprising
test: «After the storm, the sailors' escape from the rocks was miraculous.» What does miraculous mean? | Very short | Cold and wet | *Amazing, lucky and hard to explain | Dull
test: Which phrase means someone got better when nobody expected it? | A loud shout | A broken window | A slow walk | *A miraculous recovery
exam: Which sentence uses miraculous correctly? | *The footballer's miraculous escape from the crash shocked everyone | We ate miraculous sandwiches for lunch | The cup was miraculous, so I put it on the shelf | My shoes are miraculous because they are blue
